1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,784
Nineteen of the twenty-one hijacked

2
00:00:02,584 --> 00:00:05,352
N-central servers were already running

3
00:00:05,152 --> 00:00:07,530
the vendor's newest emergency fix.

4
00:00:08,230 --> 00:00:10,406
A public exploit gave attackers

5
00:00:10,206 --> 00:00:11,465
root with no login.

6
00:00:11,505 --> 00:00:13,908
Within hours, twenty-one servers were

7
00:00:13,708 --> 00:00:15,204
mining cryptocurrency.

8
00:00:15,754 --> 00:00:18,002
N-central is the console service

9
00:00:17,802 --> 00:00:19,671
providers use to run every

10
00:00:19,471 --> 00:00:20,657
client machine.

11
00:00:20,697 --> 00:00:21,757
Root on it is a

12
00:00:21,557 --> 00:00:23,334
skeleton key to all of them.

13
00:00:23,884 --> 00:00:25,910
On Monday, a researcher dumped

14
00:00:25,710 --> 00:00:27,106
more than thirty flaws.

15
00:00:27,146 --> 00:00:28,810
Tuesday brought Hotfix 2.

16
00:00:28,850 --> 00:00:30,593
On Thursday, a new chain

17
00:00:30,393 --> 00:00:30,996
beat it.

18
00:00:31,036 --> 00:00:32,773
Friday, still no patch.

19
00:00:33,323 --> 00:00:34,914
The first attacks came at

20
00:00:34,714 --> 00:00:36,504
eight twenty-four, U T C.

21
00:00:36,544 --> 00:00:37,824
By twelve fifty,

22
00:00:37,624 --> 00:00:39,850
twenty-one mining rigs had appeared

23
00:00:39,650 --> 00:00:40,457
in one pool.

24
00:00:41,007 --> 00:00:42,746
It needs the Legacy API

25
00:00:42,546 --> 00:00:44,365
switched on and exposed.

26
00:00:44,405 --> 00:00:45,946
An old Apache Axis bug

27
00:00:45,746 --> 00:00:47,510
runs code, then a root

28
00:00:47,310 --> 00:00:49,447
helper script finishes the job.

29
00:00:49,997 --> 00:00:51,695
One firm watching the attacks

30
00:00:51,495 --> 00:00:52,415
put it plainly.

31
00:00:52,455 --> 00:00:54,293
So far the only payload

32
00:00:54,093 --> 00:00:55,587
is a Monero miner.

33
00:00:55,627 --> 00:00:57,230
That is the lucky version.

34
00:00:57,780 --> 00:01:00,269
If you host N-central yourself,

35
00:01:00,069 --> 00:01:01,822
turn off the Legacy API

36
00:01:01,622 --> 00:01:03,538
today, or put it behind

37
00:01:03,338 --> 00:01:03,947
a VPN.

38
00:01:03,987 --> 00:01:05,563
Then hunt for the miner,

39
00:01:05,363 --> 00:01:06,876
and rebuild if you find it.

40
00:01:07,426 --> 00:01:09,388
The real change is the tempo.

41
00:01:09,428 --> 00:01:11,015
A fix, a bypass two

42
00:01:10,815 --> 00:01:13,060
days later, and miners running

43
00:01:12,860 --> 00:01:15,324
before most admins read the advisory.

44
00:01:15,874 --> 00:01:17,749
The full hunting checklist is

45
00:01:17,549 --> 00:01:19,425
in the article on The Dispatch.

